  "intermediateFailures": "Initial browser boundary lacked HTMLStyleElement then TextTrackList event methods. Expanded fixture used wrong translation DOM id, left controls instead of right controls, and checked DOM before cache completion propagated. ASR restore adds existing availability metadata, so source preservation compares full restored timeline before/after and raw cache input separately. Cross-privacy cache control initially tried changing sender flags inside an already-bound private document; corrected to close synthetic ports and create distinct native documents. Node EventTarget capture removal uses the same capture options object. Old adapter algorithm/download contracts explicitly native false; new real entry/controller controls cover native true and false. First full run passed 10284 tests but exited 1 at 99.99% branches (33846/33847); initial currentSrc-empty/src-known source was not exercised. Second full run also passed 10284 tests but exited 1 at 99.99% branches (33844/33845); changing the initial fixture had replaced the no-video empty-source case. Parameterized the existing lifecycle control with both initial states without production changes. The owned-module diagnostic passed 5 tests and four-dimensional 100% before the final complete gates; it is a diagnostic, not a full-gate pass. First and second reports/inputs/metadata are preserved in separate directories; actual recorded commands retain their original paths. Third full run passed 10285 tests and four-dimensional 100% with exit 0, then the waiting tool was interrupted before a composite exit was exposed. No matching runner or subsequent completion record remained. A separately reviewed resumption found the static audit classifying six interpolated test titles as <dynamic> duplicates; its exit 1 is preserved. Converted those six tables to static format titles and Cartesian input tuples, preserving all 75 runtime controls and production bytes. Repeated the exact frozen-file baseline negative and target controls; final ten gates run against the updated test SHA, with audit/types/builds before full coverage to expose other failures sooner.",
